# INDIVIDUAL CASE SAFETY REPORT (ICSR)
## Complete Pharmacovigilance Case Assessment

### 1. Introduction

An Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR) is a structured report used in pharmacovigilance to document suspected adverse drug reactions experienced by an individual patient.

The purpose of this assessment is to identify the suspected adverse drug reaction, evaluate its relationship with the suspected medicine, classify its severity and seriousness, and prepare appropriate safety documentation.

### 2. Case Summary

**Case ID:** ICSR-001  
**Case Type:** Hypothetical case study  
**Suspected Drug:** Amoxicillin  
**Drug Class:** Penicillin Antibiotic  
**Reported Reaction:** Skin rash, redness and itching.

A 28-year-old female patient was prescribed amoxicillin for a bacterial infection. After starting the medication, she developed skin redness, itching and small red rashes over the body. The symptoms were reported following drug administration.

*Note: This is an illustrative case prepared for educational purposes.*

